<title>UK: IFC sets 12 bln yen three-year dual currency bond.</title>
<headline>IFC sets 12 bln yen three-year dual currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager LTCB International Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   INTERNATIONAL FINANCE CORP</p>
<p> AMT    12 BLN YEN    COUPON    *4.85	MATURITY   *27.JAN.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    27.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.60	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> NOTES     *PAYABLE IN YEN. REDEMPTION IN U.S. DOLLARS</p>
<p>		$4,424.78 PER 500,000 YEN.</p>
<p>		UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
